.TH "REPROCTL\-SETUP" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-setup \- bootstrap the local development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl setup\f[R] [\f[B]\(enskip\-cluster\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a 5\-step bootstrap sequence to prepare the local development
environment:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]brew bundle\f[R] \(em install Homebrew dependencies from the
Brewfile.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]proto use\f[R] \(em activate the correct toolchain versions.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]pnpm install\f[R] \(em install Node.js dependencies.
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Docker check\f[R] \(em verify Docker is running.
.IP "5." 3
\f[B]cluster up\f[R] \(em create the local kind cluster and container
registry.
.PP
Each step is idempotent and safe to re\-run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-cluster\f[R]
Skip step 5 (kind cluster creation).
Useful when you only need to update dependencies without touching the
cluster.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl setup
Run the full bootstrap sequence.
.TP
reproctl setup \(enskip\-cluster
Bootstrap without creating the cluster.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-doctor\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-cluster\f[R](1)
